// Deepseek did not answer -- timed out, refused, or returned nothing usable.
// Emits the exact envelope Parse Deepseek Response expects, so every node
// downstream keeps working and the intake is written and alerted instead of
// vanishing. Added 2026-08-08, carried from Brasa's assurance item 11.
//
// service_category is deliberately a string ch_services does not contain, so
// Parse degrades it to the non-assignable fallback AND forces confidence_flag
// true -> needs_review true. Two independent reasons a human sees it.
//
// urgency_level 3 is a deliberate over-band, and it is not free: a provider
// outage will raise acute-banded alerts for routine enquiries. For a clinic the
// asymmetry is not close -- an unread acute message costs more than an
// over-banded routine one -- and ADR-2 already alerts on every level, so this
// changes how urgently someone is told, never whether.
return [{ json: {
  choices: [{ message: { content: JSON.stringify({
    service_category:   'Model unavailable',
    urgency_level:      3,
    complexity:         'high',
    recommended_action: 'The classifier did not respond. This intake has not been '
                      + 'triaged by the model and needs a human to read it.',
    confidence_flag:    true
  }) } }],
  usage: { prompt_tokens: 0, completion_tokens: 0, total_tokens: 0 },
  model_unavailable: true
} }];
